  note = {Paris: Les Editions de Minuit, 1984. A probing inquiry into how we make sense of frame-crossing and counterfactual statements of this sort: "If Clark Gable had been a woman, Scarlett O'Hara would have been a man". Full of ideas about reference, identity, slippability, and essence.}
